desc:
This course is intended for those who wish to write a master's thesis on Child Language Aquisition.

The course provides in-depth knowledge and skills in planning, conducting, and presenting an independent research project in the field of Child Language Aquisition.

Teaching format:
Teaching is conducted through seminars and supervision.

Assessment:
The course is assessed through:

a written project proposal specifying the thesis topic;

a written thesis presenting the student's completed research project;

a defense of the student's own thesis;

an opposition on another student's thesis;

active participation in seminar discussions.
